{"name":"Georgian Bay","hex":"#22657f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Georgian Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large bay off Lake Huron, within Ontario, Canada.","A township in Muskoka district municipality, south-central Ontario, named after the bay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Georgian_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Georgian Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Georgian Bay is a large bay of Lake Huron. It is located entirely within the borders of Ontario, Canada. The main body of the bay lies east of the Bruce Peninsula and Manitoulin Island. To its northwest is the North Channel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Boulder_Beach_3.jpg/330px-Boulder_Beach_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian_Bay","wikidata":"Q1267413"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Great_Lakes_Lake_Huron_Georgian_Bay.png/500px-Great_Lakes_Lake_Huron_Georgian_Bay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Great_Lakes_Lake_Huron_Georgian_Bay.png/500px-Great_Lakes_Lake_Huron_Georgian_Bay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Main body of Georgian Bay highlighted on the map of the Great Lakes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreat_Lakes_Lake_Huron_Georgian_Bay.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Tom_Thomson_-_Pine_Island%2C_Georgian_Bay.jpg/330px-Tom_Thomson_-_Pine_Island%2C_Georgian_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Tom_Thomson_-_Pine_Island%2C_Georgian_Bay.jpg/330px-Tom_Thomson_-_Pine_Island%2C_Georgian_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tom Thomson, Pine Island, Georgian Bay, Winter 1914–16. National Gallery of Canada, Ottawa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATom_Thomson_-_Pine_Island%2C_Georgian_Bay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/BeausoleilIslandCedarSprings2004.jpg/500px-BeausoleilIslandCedarSprings2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/BeausoleilIslandCedarSprings2004.jpg/500px-BeausoleilIslandCedarSprings2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t